{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`tests/integration/test_fold_cross_clone_horizon.py` failed in 3 of the Nov 19-20 2026 local `make verify` runs on oversubscribed hosts and passes in CI: `test_snapshot_repair_on_stale_clone_keeps_concurrent_tag` with \"SETUP: the merge must land B's tag\" (verify-willet.log) and \"SETUP: A must hold a COMMENT orphan to repair\" (bug-create-replay make-verify.log), and `test_fold_on_stale_clone_keeps_concurrent_tag` (fix-ref-lock-test-bound). Both are setup assertions, not the behavior under test.\n\n## Root cause (verified)\nEach test drives two clones through real `rebar` child processes and then reads the other clone's writes with an explicit `git fetch origin tickets`. Those writes reach origin only through rebar's post-write push, which is best-effort by design: `push_tickets_branch` bounds `git push` at `_GIT_TIMEOUT = 30` s and a timeout never fails the write (`src/rebar/_store/push.py`). A timed-out push is retried (3 attempts with 0.5 s and 2.0 s backoff), but on a starved host every attempt can exceed 30 s; the write still exits 0 and the next fetch does not contain it, so the setup precondition fails. The tests already turn the best-effort read sync into a checked precondition (`_sync_from_origin`), but rely on the best-effort push succeeding.\n\nDeterministic reproduction (Nov 20 2026, origin/main 8e1d15e664f): a PATH `git` shim that sleeps 32 s before any `git push` makes every best-effort push time out. `test_snapshot_repair_on_stale_clone_keeps_concurrent_tag` then fails at setup every run (here clone B cannot see A's unpublished ticket: `rebar comment ... Error: ticket '...' not found`); without the shim it passes.\n\n## Approach\nMake delivery a checked precondition, mirroring how `_sync_from_origin` makes the read side checked: add a `_publish(tracker)` helper in the test module that runs a checked `git push -q origin HEAD:tickets` from that clone's tracker (a no-op when the best-effort push already landed), and call it after every write whose arrival at origin a later fetch depends on: A's create and comment (read by B's `_sync_from_origin`), B's comment (read by A's fetch before the merge), and B's tag edit (read by A's final fetch). No other write is read cross-clone: A's `store compact ... --skip-sync` never pushes (`src/rebar/_commands/compact.py`, the `not skip_sync` guard before `push_after_commit`), so B's second `_sync_from_origin` in the repair test reads only those published writes, and A's later writes are only read by A. The helper's docstring says why (best-effort production push, 30 s bound with retries). The behavior under test (fold and snapshot repair placement, orphan detection) is unchanged, and no product code changes.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/integration/test_fold_cross_clone_horizon.py`\n\n## Testing\n- Reproduction harness: under the 32 s push shim each rebar write spends about 92 s in its retried push and each `_publish` about 32 s, so the shim runs pass `-o timeout=1800` on the pytest command line to lift the 300 s per-test budget for that run only; the module carries no new marker. Under the shim both tests pass after the change (they fail before it), runs recorded on this ticket.\n- Without the shim both tests still pass.\n- The module's existing assertions on SNAPSHOT placement, tag survival and fsck orphan rows are unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Both fold cross-clone tests pass under the 32 s push shim (with `-o timeout=1800`) and without it (default budget), runs recorded here.\n- [ ] Every cross-clone read in the module follows a checked publish of the write it depends on.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes on the change and Gerrit gives Verified +1."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795208333028510001,"uuid":"57ae62de-1370-48ab-a979-69622be8cc6b"}